# Frontend

## Design System

Follow `DESIGN-stripe.md`: indigo primary (`#533afd`), ink body text (`#0d253d`), pill buttons, gradient-mesh heroes, thin (300) display type with negative tracking, Inter as Sohne substitute.

- Money and numeric values: use tabular figures (`font-feature-settings: "tnum"`)
- Cards on near-white surfaces; dashboard areas may use dark navy (`#1c1e54`) shell
- Preserve responsive/mobile behavior (breakpoints at 768px / 1024px)

## Wallet & Blockchain

- Use **Stellar Wallet Kit** (`@stellar/wallet-kit`) — support Freighter, Albedo, xBull minimum
- Wrap wallet flows to normalize popup/redirect/deep-link differences per provider
- Clearly distinguish: disconnected, connecting, connected, signing, rejected, error states
- Use Soroban RPC (`rpc.Server`) for contract calls — not Horizon for contract interactions
- Soroban/Testnet state is authoritative — do not fake financial or blockchain state in production UI

## UX Requirements

- Show loading, success, rejection, and error states for all on-chain actions
- Test wallet rejection and insufficient-balance flows per supported provider
- Keep private metadata (client details, documents) separate from on-chain display

## Security & Config

- Do not expose secrets in client-side code
- Use environment variables for public config (e.g. `NEXT_PUBLIC_TOKEN_CONTRACT_ADDRESS`)
- Never hard-code private keys, secrets, or credentials
